assignment_uuid#:#UUID
assignment_uuid_info#:#The UUID is assigned by the container service to this exercise unit when the Dockerfile and provided files are uploaded to create the container image. It is used when grading submissions to identify this exercise unit.
provided_files#:#Provided Files
purpose#:#Purpose
purpose_docker#:#Dockerfile
purpose_docker_info#:#Command file for Docker to create a container image for grading this exercise. There may only be one Dockerfile per exercise unit. Upload additional required files after creating this exercise unit on the "Provided Files" tab.
purpose_support#:#Setup
purpose_support_info#:#Support file used to create the container image. Multiple files of this type are passed compressed with gzip when setting up the grading (extension .tgz). If this file is changed, the container image becomes invalid and the grading must be set up again. All already submitted submissions will be reset.
purpose_submit#:#Grading
purpose_submit_info#:#Support file used to grade an assignment. Files of this type are passed compressed with gzip with each grading along with the student submission (extension .tgz). If this file is changed, the container image remains valid, but already submitted submissions will be reset.
purpose_ignore#:#Ignored
purpose_ignore_info#:#Files of this type are not sent to the grading service. They can be templates for students, for example.
purpose_example#:#Sample Solution
purpose_example_info#:#File of a sample solution. Students must upload a file with this name. This file is used to test the functioning of the grading. Multiple files of this type are passed to the container service compressed with gzip (extension .tgz).
file_description_info#:#If the file is public, the description is also displayed to students.
is_public_info#:#The file is offered to students for download along with the assignment.
